      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanadium substitution will refine the grain structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanadium substitution may produce nanoscale local ordering or subtle precipitates.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed local ordering or precipitates will not disrupt overall BCC stability.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Greater lattice-distortion heterogeneity will promote low-temperature dislocation mobility and thereby improve ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lattice distortion can restrict irradiation-induced defect-cluster formation and growth.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456733::web::022::3_4_irradiation_hardening"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Structural disorder in high-entropy alloys can facilitate recombination or annihilation of irradiation-induced vacancies and interstitials.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456733::web::022::3_4_irradiation_hardening",
        "PMC11396103::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanadium micro-alloying will preserve a dominant BCC phase in NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanadium-doped NbMoTaW will have greater room-temperature tensile elongation and reduced brittleness than untreated NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanadium-doped NbMoTaW will have smaller helium bubbles and lower irradiation-induced defect density than untreated NbMoTaW.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456733::web::022::3_4_irradiation_hardening",
        "PMC11396103::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanadium-doped NbMoTaW will retain high-temperature strength comparable to untreated NbMoTaW up to 1600 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted irradiation benefit applies under helium-ion fluences representative of reactor environments.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hypothesis is falsified if vanadium-doped NbMoTaW lacks a statistically significant ductility improvement, loses high-temperature strength, or exhibits increased irradiation-induced defect clustering relative to pristine NbMoTaW.",
